COMMON RULES (paste above every prompt)
CONTEXT: Motion.Pulse is an XML Views app (single Activity, Fragments, Navigation Component, ViewBinding,
Hilt). No Compose exists in the project any more. A migration left the screens as empty shells: the header
image shows, but the content, features and behavior of the old screens are missing.

SOURCE OF TRUTH: the last Compose version is in git. Use the tag pre-compose-removal (if that tag does not
contain files under app/src/main/java/com/example/motionpulse/ui/screens, use commit 7f8eed9). Find files with
`git ls-tree -r --name-only pre-compose-removal app/src/main/java` and read them with
`git show pre-compose-removal:<path>`. The old code wins over this prompt's checklist if they differ. Tell me
about every difference.

RULES:
1. Never mark a feature done unless it is built, wired to real data and you ran it. No placeholders, no TODO,
   no "coming soon", no hard-coded sample data.
2. If a ViewModel or repository function the screen needs is missing or was changed, restore it from the old
   code. Do not change Firestore rules, indexes or tests unless this prompt says so.
3. XML + ViewBinding + Fragment. Set the binding to null in onDestroyView. Collect flows with
   viewLifecycleOwner.lifecycleScope + repeatOnLifecycle(STARTED). Navigate through the nav graph.
4. Look: reuse the tokens in colors.xml and the shared views (DropletHeaderView, UserAvatarView,
   MoodPillView, StateLayout, the bottom nav). Cards: solid #1C0620, 1dp stroke #E01E79, 20dp corners.
5. Adaptive: dp and sp, ConstraintLayout/wrap_content, no fixed heights around text, scrolling for overflow,
   48dp touch targets, texts in strings.xml, contentDescription on icon-only views. Check sw320dp and font
   scales 1.3 and 2.0. Headers scroll away with the content and the bottom nav stays.
6. Never write an empty catch block. Log every caught exception with its real message.
7. Work in this order and keep going until it is finished: (a) read the old code and the screen's section in
   MIGRATION_PARITY.md, (b) build the layouts, (c) build adapters and custom views, (d) wire to the
   ViewModel, (e) run the app and exercise every feature, (f) update the statuses in MIGRATION_PARITY.md.
8. Do not commit. Do not start another screen. Finish with a parity table: feature | built | tested | note..artifacts/
